<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλλω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
			5.35
		</span></i>, aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσκῡλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
				</span></i>
			(v. infr.):—
				Pass.
			, v. infr.; aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκύλθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					769.41
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				1516.57
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκύλην [ῠ</span>] (v.
			infr.): pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσκυλμαι</span> (v. infr.):—=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ὄνυξι σπᾶν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; aor.
			inf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοῦλαι</span> (perh. 
				Lacon.
			),= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνῆσαι</span>, Id.:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλλονται</span>, of dead
			bodies <i>torn</i> by fish, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				577
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσκυλται . . κίκιννος</span>”
				<i>is dishevelled,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					5.174
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσκυλται δὲ κόμη</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				258
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>maltreat, molest</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἐν [τοῖς ἱεροῖς] ἀποτεταγμένους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sammelb.</u>
					6236.22
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃς δὲ ἂν σκύλῃ
				[τὸ μνῆμα</span>] <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1901
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Rome</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				3.6
			</span></i> (Inscr. Cyzic.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3757
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nicaea</span>), <i><span class="en">
				4077
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Ancyra</span>):—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				107.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>trouble, annoy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀσθενοῦσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλας καὶ ὑβρίσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					7.3.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τὸν στρατόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.13.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί σκύλλεις τὸν
			διδάσκαλον</span>; <u>Ev.Marc.</u> l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				8.49
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλον σεαυτὸν πρὸς ἡμᾶς φέρων
				. . τὴν ὕαλον</span>
			<i>bestir</i> yourself (i.e. <i>hurry</i>) to us with . . ,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>PFay.</u>
				134.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>:—
				Pass.
			 and 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ σκύλλου</span>
			<i>trouble</i> not <i>thyself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Luc.
				7.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυλῆναι πρὸς Τιμόθεον</span>
			<i>take the trouble to go</i> to T., <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				123.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκυλῆναι
				ἀνέξεται</span>; will he <i>trouble to come?</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phoeb.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				p.44S.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῦλαι</span> (imper. 
				Med.
			) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεαυτὸν καὶ κτλ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PBaden</u>
				33.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκυλμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					9.36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλλεται καὶ καταπονεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diog.Oen.
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλαιο κάρη</span>
			<i>shave</i> the patient's head, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				410
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
